RuntimeSchema: EightD KG Current Runtime Contract for Django
SchemaVersion: v0.1.0
PipelineVersion: pipeline-v0.1.0
Language: en
Audience: Django integration engineers

Summary:
  This file describes the current runtime schema and ontology that are actually enforced by the 8D KG service today.
  It is the integration-facing runtime contract, not the full product ontology backlog.

CanonicalRuntimeSources:
  VersionSource: backend/app/core/versioning.py
  ExtractionSchemaRoot: backend/app/schemas/extraction.py
  RuntimeEntitySubset: backend/app/schemas/entity.py
  GraphAllowList: backend/app/graph/client.py
  FullOntologyBaseline: docs/SCHEMA.md

VersionRules:
  Active schema_version is derived from backend/app/core/versioning.py.
  Active pipeline_version is derived from backend/app/core/versioning.py.
  If this file and runtime code ever diverge, runtime code is authoritative until the docs are updated.

ExtractionContract:
  RootModel: ExtractionResult
  RequiredShape:
    report: EightDReport | null
    event: ProductEvent | null
    failure_modes: FailureMode[]
    causes: CauseItem[]
    actions: ActionItem[]
    product_instances: ProductInstance[]
    part_serials: PartSerial[]
    organizations: Organization[]
    persons: Person[]
    failure_products: FailureProduct[]
    failure_product_mentions: FailureProductMention[]
    relationships: RelationTriple[]
    chunks: Chunk[]
    stats: dict

RuntimeEntityTypes:
  - EightDReport
  - ProductEvent
  - FailureMode
  - CauseItem
  - ActionItem
  - ProductInstance
  - PartSerial
  - Organization
  - Person
  - FailureProduct
  - FailureProductMention
  - Chunk

GraphOntology:
  AllowedLabels:
    - EightDReport
    - ProductEvent
    - ProductInstance
    - PartSerial
    - FailureMode
    - CauseItem
    - ActionItem
    - Organization
    - Person
    - FailureProduct
    - FailureProductMention
    - Chunk
  AllowedRelationshipTypes:
    - HAS_8D_REPORT
    - RELATED_FAILURE_MODE
    - ROOT_CAUSE
    - CORRECTIVE_ACTION
    - PREVENTIVE_ACTION
    - VERIFIES_CAUSE
    - HAPPENED_ON
    - RELATED_SERIAL
    - AFFECTED_PRODUCT
    - AFFECTED_SERIAL
    - RESPONSIBLE_ORG
    - INVOLVES_PERSON
    - AUTHORED_BY_PERSON
    - REVIEWED_BY_PERSON
    - REPORTED_BY_PERSON
    - OWNED_BY_PERSON
    - TARGET_SERIAL
    - TARGET_PRODUCT
    - INSTALLED_ON
    - SUPPLIED_BY
    - MENTIONED_IN
    - MENTIONS
    - CHUNK_OF_REPORT
    - MENTIONS_FAILURE_PRODUCT
    - INSTANCE_OF_FAILURE_PRODUCT

InterpretationRules:
  docs/SCHEMA.md is the full ontology baseline and design intent.
  backend/app/schemas/extraction.py plus backend/app/schemas/entity.py define the current runtime extraction subset.
  backend/app/graph/client.py is the final graph admission gate.
  Django integration should depend on this runtime contract, not on non-runtime ontology sections.

IntegrationGuidance:
  Use the integration facade as the only external entry point.
  Expect only the entity types and relationship types listed above.
  Do not assume that every entity or relationship from docs/SCHEMA.md is implemented at runtime.
  Treat this file as the current runtime snapshot for API and downstream mapping work.